# EVI dev bridge

- **EVI (`agent-api`)**: runtime productivity — tools, `/chat`, webhooks, notes, WhatsApp processor tests.
- **Dev bridge** (`agent/services/dev_bridge.py`, `agent/devcli/`): implement/refactor this repo remotely from WhatsApp/Telegram control chat — `dev: <desc>` → `dev approve <id>`. Only when `EVI_DEV_BRIDGE_ENABLED=true`. CLI backend selected via `EVI_DEV_CLI` (default `claude`); adding a new backend is a new module in `agent/devcli/` plus one line in `resolve_dev_cli` (`agent/devcli/factory.py`) — the propose/approve core never changes.
- **Copilot CLI**: `scripts/copilot-dev-runner.sh` for explain/scaffold/debug — standalone, not wired into the dev bridge, not for user-facing agent replies.

See [docs/dev-workflow.md](../../docs/dev-workflow.md).
